name issue_151_outage_3s_v2
describe 3 s outage with all v2 switches on: the receiver stops NACKing what a keyframe made moot (issue #151)
cc v2
pacer v2
tcc v2
rtx v2
rtcp v2
keyframe v2
allocator v2
packetization v2
audio v2
seed 1
duration 30s
at 0s  capacity=1500kbps delay=30ms queue=300ms
at 12s down
at 15s up
reverse at 0s delay=30ms
reverse at 12s down
reverse at 15s up
# Receiver NACK give-up (issue #151). Before the fix the receiver re-requested the ~60 packets lost in the outage
# every 20 ms for 2 s after the keyframe had been decoded (100 NACK batches, 47 useless retransmissions that
# queued behind the recovery keyframe); libwebrtc's NackRequester::ClearUpTo drops them at the first continuous
# frame (one burst, 17 RTX).
# Seeds 1-3 on main 3179f13: repair.overhead_pct 1.44 / 1.75 / 1.61, video.freeze_total_ms 4093 / 4084 / 4118;
# with the fix 1.34 / 1.37 / 1.33 and 4070 / 4034 / 4072.
# Target (issue #151): cc.queue_p95_ms < 40 (libwebrtc 39), freeze total within the parity band of libwebrtc (3217).
expect repair.overhead_pct < 1.4
expect video.freeze_total_ms < 4080
